    "turn_text": "It was. Again, you know, we are of the Republican Party on, you know, my side. And again, we have John Bill A. We're a Democrat and, you know, I like John Bill. We are, you know, good acquaintances. But again, because of the difference of politics, there are different ideas of how things can be done, should be done, and how it will be done. And certainly, you know, if you have watched my congressional record, you know, pro-life, pro-gun, very conservative, fiscally. And, you know, I saw the state, again, go in a direction where, you know, debt wasn't mounting up. Some of the social issues were somewhat of things that I disagreed with. And, you know, our businesses were leaving the state in droves. Look at what our oil and gas industry is at this time. I mean, oil prices are in the tank. The oil and gas industry is still pretty much the lifeline and the umbilical cord of the Louisiana economy. We have other great businesses, certainly in Louisiana. But if you take away our oil and gas, then we're somewhat dead in the water. Again, a lot of civil litigation against our oil and gas companies right now. And these were things that, you know, I thought that if elected, you know, I would address and perhaps, you know, do it a different",
