    "turn_text": "I promised when I ran the first time that I would run only three terms and then either run for another office or, you know, get out. I am a firm firm believer. in term limits. The founders never meant for a member of Congress to make a career out of being a politician. We have people up in Congress now and these are good people but they have been there sometimes decades and I just disagree with that concept. I think fresh blood is good in politics, fresh ideas, fresh people because that's the way not only a economy grows, but it's the way a country grows. And I figure we can become stagnated if we have the same people in the same job doing the same thing over and over.",
