    "turn_idx": 44,
    "turn_text": "I met President Trump when he was candidate Trump back in Washington DC. It was an odd event. Him and Ted Cruz at that time were somewhat campaigning together, and that was very early in the presidential campaign. And, you know, Hardy was there, so I ran over and, you know, met each other's hands. We exchanged some pleasantries, but as far as getting to know him, it was not until after he was elected, and I was elected. President Trump is, you know, like and disliking what I can tell you personally, he's a good man. He cares about the country. He's no, he's not politically correct. He doesn't really care. He's a New Yorker. He's a developer, a real estate man from New York, and he's tough as a boot. And if you give him some grief, he's going to give you some back. But that's what I like about President Trump. He is not that politician that we envision being a president of the United States. This is a guy that's able to stand on his own He will defend himself and his family with his last breath, but he will also defend his country with his last breath. I've seen him in very, he did debates in a very small environment and his factual base is vast. He's a very intelligent man and I just like him. I like what he stands for and I like that he doesn't take any growth. from anybody else, on either side of the political aisle.",
